BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 384.0 Tm (On the evening of 16 July 1999, a small single engine plane took off from) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 370.4 Tm (New Jersey. It was heading for Martha\222s Vineyard. The pilot was) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 356.8 Tm (experienced enough to be confident and new enough to be wrong about what) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 343.2 Tm (that confidence meant. He had about 300 hours in the air. He had not) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 329.6 Tm (finished the training that would qualify him to fly using only his instruments.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 308.0 Tm (The sky was clear when he departed so he concluded that he did not need) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 294.4 Tm (instruments. By the time he reached the coast, a haze had settled over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 280.8 Tm (water. The mist came, the one that erases the line between sea and sky so) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 267.2 Tm (gradually that you do not notice the horizon is gone until you look for it and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 253.6 Tm (it is not there. Over land there are lights below. You see roads, buildings, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 240.0 Tm (geometry that tells your eyes which way is down. Over open water at night,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 226.4 Tm (with haze sitting on the surface like a second darkness, there is nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 212.8 Tm (The world outside the cockpit becomes a uniform grey in every direction. Up) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 199.2 Tm (looks like down. A gentle turn feels like level flight. A slow descent feels) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 185.6 Tm (like holding steady.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 164.0 Tm (The pilot\222s inner ear, the organ that tells the brain which way the body is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 150.4 Tm (oriented in space, works by detecting changes in motion. When you enter a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 136.8 Tm (turn, the fluid inside the ear shifts, and the brain registers rotation. But if) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 123.2 Tm (the turn holds steady for fifteen or twenty seconds, the fluid in the inner ear) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 109.6 Tm (settles. It stops moving. The brain, which tracks movement, concludes that) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 96.0 Tm (the turn has ended. You feel level, but you are not.) Tj ET
endstream
