BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 572.0 Tm (Somewhere over the dark water, the plane entered a gentle left turn. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 558.4 Tm (pilot\222s instruments, the dials on the panel in front of him, showed the turn.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 544.8 Tm (The artificial horizon, a small gyroscope display that shows the aircraft\222s) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 531.2 Tm (angle relative to the earth, was telling him clearly that he was banking. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 517.6 Tm (altimeter was telling him he was descending. The airspeed indicator was) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 504.0 Tm (telling him he was accelerating. His body was telling him something different.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 490.4 Tm (His body was telling him he was flying straight and level. His body felt right.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 476.8 Tm (His instruments felt wrong. He trusted his body.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 455.2 Tm (Then turn tightened. The nose dropped. The airspeed built. In the final) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 441.6 Tm (seconds, the plane was descending at more than 4,700 feet per minute,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 428.0 Tm (nearly a mile every sixty seconds, in a tightening spiral that pilots call, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 414.4 Tm (the grim precision of a profession that has named the ways it loses people, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 400.8 Tm (graveyard spiral. He hit the water at full speed. He and his two passengers) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 387.2 Tm (were killed on impact.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 365.6 Tm (The investigation found no mechanical failure. The engine was running. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 352.0 Tm (instruments were working. The data was right there, on the panel, six inches) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 338.4 Tm (from his eyes, the whole time, but he did not read it. He read his body) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 324.8 Tm (instead. The American Federal Aviation Administration\222s instruction to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 311.2 Tm (pilots who find themselves in this situation is one sentence long. It is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 297.6 Tm (literal instruction that applies to your life as directly as it applies to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 284.0 Tm (cockpit:) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 90 258.4 Tm (\223have confidence in your instruments and ignore all conflicting) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 90 244.8 Tm (signals your body gives you.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 219.2 Tm (The pilot\222s name was John F. Kennedy Jr. He was the son of an American) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 205.6 Tm (president. He had been advised not to fly that night without his instructor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 192.0 Tm (He told his instructor he wanted to do it alone. He was thirty-eight years old.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 170.4 Tm (You operate a body that produces signals and your mind often treats those) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 156.8 Tm (signals as truth. The signals are sometimes as wrong as the inner ear\222s) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 143.2 Tm (vestibular system over dark water. The tiredness that presents itself as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 129.6 Tm (question about your career. The caffeine spike that presents itself as) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 116.0 Tm (anxiety about an email. The low blood sugar that presents itself as evidence) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 102.4 Tm (that your relationship is failing. Your body speaks first and your mind) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 88.8 Tm (explains second. The explanation, because it comes with the full weight of) Tj ET
endstream
